# Desktop app PRODUCTION environment variables.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.production` and fill in the real production API
# URL BEFORE running `pnpm --filter @msph/desktop build` (which is what
# `pnpm --filter @msph/desktop dist` also runs before packaging the
# Windows/macOS/Linux installer). Vite automatically loads `.env.production`
# for any `vite build` (mode "production") — no extra flag needed.
#
# If this is missing or empty when you build, the packaged app will show
# a clear "Erreur de configuration" screen on startup instead of silently
# trying localhost (see src/config.ts) — that is the intended fail-safe,
# not a bug, but you still need to set this correctly before shipping.
#
# Must be HTTPS in a real deployment (see README.md "Production domain").

VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.your-production-domain.example

# Optional — only needed if Socket.IO should point somewhere other than
# VITE_API_BASE_URL with its trailing /api stripped.
# VITE_SOCKET_URL=https://api.your-production-domain.example
